quiz.q:
A function reads lines of the form `name age` into `person p[static 20]` and must return the number of lines in the file even if there are more than 20. Here is its loop. Find the bug and fix it.

```c
while (fgets(line, 100, f) != NULL) {
    sscanf(line, "%19s %d", p[n].name, &p[n].age);
    n++;
}
```

quiz.answer:
When the file has more than 20 lines, `p[n]` with `n >= 20` writes past the end of the array. Parse into a temporary and store only if there is room:

```c
while (fgets(line, 100, f) != NULL) {
    person tmp;
    if (sscanf(line, "%19s %d", tmp.name, &tmp.age) == 2 && n < 20) {
        p[n] = tmp;
    }
    n++;
}
```

